/given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Genetic variability in G protein gene of Group A and B respiratory syncytial viruses from India.</article-title><source>J of Clin Microbiol</source><volume>44</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>3055</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16954227</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Parveen2"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parveen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Broor</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapoor</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Fowler</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullender</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Genetic diversity among respiratory syncytial viruses that have caused repeated infections in children from rural India.</article-title><source>J Med Virol</source><volume>78</volume><fpage>659</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16555275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Shann1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shann</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Steinhoff</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Vaccines for children in rich and poor countries.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>354</volume><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10406357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-BoshciPinto1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boshci-Pinto</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tomaskovic</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><collab>CHERG (Child Health Epidemiology Reference Group)</collab><year>2002</year><source>First Meeting 6&#x02013;7 February 2002.</source><publisher-loc>La Mainaz, Gex, France</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Child Health and Development, Department of Child and Adolescent Health and Development, World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-CHERG1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>CHERG (Child Health Epidemiology Reference Group)</collab><year>2001</year><source>Urbanization patterns and rural population growth at the country level: United Nations Population Division 50-74.</source></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Robertson1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Roca</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Respiratory syncytial virus infection: denominator-based studies in Indonesia, Mozambique, Nigeria and South Africa.</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><volume>82</volume><fpage>914</fpage><lpage>922</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15654405</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Selwyn1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Selwyn</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>The epidemiology of acute respiratory tract infection in young children: comparison of findings from several developing countries.</article-title><source>Rev of Infect Dis</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>S870</fpage><lpage>S888</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2270410</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Glezen1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glezen</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name><name><surname>Taber</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasel</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Risk of primary infection and reinfection with respiratory syncytial virus.</article-title><source>Am J Dis Child</source><volume>140</volume><fpage>543</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3706232</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Nokes1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nokes</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Okiro</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ngama</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ochola</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Respiratory syncytial virus epidemiology in a birth cohort from Kilifi district, Kenya: infection during the first year of life.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>190</volume><fpage>1828</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15499540</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Jennings1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jennings</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><name><surname>Werno</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Beynon</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Murdoch</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Viral etiology of acute respiratory tract infections in children presenting to hospital: role of polymerase chain reaction and demonstration of multiple infections.</article-title><source>Pediatr Infect Dis J</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>1003</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15545854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Wolontis1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolontis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Stenbeck</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fransen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>1969</year><article-title>Multiple virus isolations in a group of children hospitalized with acute respiratory illness.</article-title><source>Scandinavian J of Infect Dis</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>26</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Hillis1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hillis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bang</surname><given-names>FB</given-names></name><name><surname>Dey</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>KV</given-names></name></person-group><year>1971</year><article-title>Respiratory syncytial virus infection in children in West Bengal.</article-title><source>Indian J Med Res</source><volume>59</volume><fpage>1354</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5161563</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000491-Henderson1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Collier</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Clyde</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Denny</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>1979</year><article-title>Respiratory syncytial virus infections, reinfections and immunity.</article-title><source>N Eng J Med</source><volume>300</volume><fp